  ('rookie-01', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'A game has just started and you have won the first two points, so your score is 30. What is your score called if you also win the next point?', '[{"id":"a","label":"45"},{"id":"b","label":"40"},{"id":"c","label":"Game"},{"id":"d","label":"Advantage"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'Point scores are called love, 15, 30 and 40, so a third point takes you to 40. You need one more point after 40 to win the game, unless the score reaches deuce.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-02', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'The server has won two points and the receiver has won one. How should the score be called?', '[{"id":"a","label":"30–15"},{"id":"b","label":"15–30"},{"id":"c","label":"30–all"},{"id":"d","label":"40–15"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'The server''s score is always called first. Two points is 30 and one point is 15, so the call is 30–15.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-03', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In a game with standard advantage scoring, both players have won three points. What is the score called?', '[{"id":"a","label":"40–30"},{"id":"b","label":"Advantage to the server"},{"id":"c","label":"Game to whoever won the most recent point"},{"id":"d","label":"Deuce"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'Three points each is called deuce. From deuce, a player must win two points in a row to win the game.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-04', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'At deuce, the receiver wins the next point. Then the server wins the point after that. What is the score now?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Game to the receiver"},{"id":"b","label":"Advantage to the server"},{"id":"c","label":"Deuce"},{"id":"d","label":"40–30 to the receiver"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'Winning the point at deuce gives the receiver advantage. When the server wins the next point, that advantage is lost and the score returns to deuce.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-05', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'Your first serve hits the net and lands outside the service box. Your second serve lands beyond the service line. What happens?', '[{"id":"a","label":"You get another first serve because the ball touched the net"},{"id":"b","label":"The point is replayed as a let"},{"id":"c","label":"You lose the point because of a double fault"},{"id":"d","label":"You serve again from the other half of the court"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'A let only applies when a serve touches the net and then lands in the correct service box, so your first serve was a fault. Two faults in a row is a double fault, and the server loses the point.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-06', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'You are serving the first point of a game from behind the baseline, just right of the center mark. Where must the serve land to be good?', '[{"id":"a","label":"In the service box straight ahead of you, on the same side of the court"},{"id":"b","label":"In the service box diagonally across the net from you"},{"id":"c","label":"Anywhere in your opponent''s singles court"},{"id":"d","label":"Anywhere between the opponent''s service line and baseline"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'Each game starts with a serve from the right half of the court. The serve must land in the service box diagonally opposite, including its lines.', '{"player":{"x":55,"y":97},"opponent":{"x":30,"y":3},"caption":"You stand behind your baseline at the bottom of the court, just right of the center mark. The receiver waits behind the far baseline on the left side of the diagram, diagonally across from you."}'::jsonb, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-07', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'Your set uses standard rules: first to 6 games with a 2-game lead, and a tie-break at 6 games all. Which game score ends the set without a tie-break?', '[{"id":"a","label":"6–5"},{"id":"b","label":"5–3"},{"id":"c","label":"6–6"},{"id":"d","label":"7–5"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'A set needs at least 6 games and a 2-game lead. At 6–5 play continues, so the set ends 7–5 or goes to a tie-break at 6–6.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-08', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In a tie-break, the score is 7–6. What happens next?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Play continues, because a player must lead by at least 2 points"},{"id":"b","label":"The player on 7 points wins the set"},{"id":"c","label":"One sudden-death point decides the set"},{"id":"d","label":"The tie-break resets to 0–0"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'A tie-break is won by the first player to reach 7 points with a 2-point lead. At 7–6 nobody has won yet, so play continues until someone leads by two, such as 8–6 or 10–8.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-09', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'You serve the first point of a tie-break. Who serves points 2 and 3?', '[{"id":"a","label":"You serve both"},{"id":"b","label":"Your opponent serves both"},{"id":"c","label":"Your opponent serves point 2 and you serve point 3"},{"id":"d","label":"Whoever won point 1 serves both"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'The first server serves one point, then the players take turns serving two points each. Your opponent serves points 2 and 3, you serve points 4 and 5, and so on.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-10', 'rookie', 'rules', 3, 'During a tie-break, when do the players change ends?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Each time the server changes"},{"id":"b","label":"Only when the score reaches 6–6"},{"id":"c","label":"After every six points, and again when the tie-break ends"},{"id":"d","label":"They never change ends during a tie-break"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'Players change ends after every six points of a tie-break, which keeps conditions such as sun and wind fair. They also change ends when the tie-break is over.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-100', 'rookie', 'rules', 3, 'In junior drill scenario 90, what is the correct rule for rally shot stays in net?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Replay"},{"id":"b","label":"Ball remains live"},{"id":"c","label":"Opponent loses point"},{"id":"d","label":"The hitter loses the point"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'A player loses the point when their shot does not cross the net into the opponent’s court.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-101', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In junior drill scenario 91, what is the correct rule for returning a serve?', '[{"id":"a","label":"The receiver must let the serve bounce"},{"id":"b","label":"Receiver may volley it"},{"id":"c","label":"Server may catch it"},{"id":"d","label":"It must bounce twice"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'The receiver must allow the serve to bounce before returning it.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-102', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In junior drill scenario 92, what is the correct rule for serving sides?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Left side first always"},{"id":"b","label":"Right side first, then alternate"},{"id":"c","label":"Any side"},{"id":"d","label":"Middle only"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'A game starts with service from the right side, then the server alternates sides each point.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-103', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In junior drill scenario 93, what is the correct rule for change of ends?', '[{"id":"a","label":"After every point"},{"id":"b","label":"Only after each set"},{"id":"c","label":"After odd-numbered games"},{"id":"d","label":"After even-numbered games"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'Players normally change ends after odd-numbered games.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-104', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In junior drill scenario 94, what is the correct rule for set tiebreak timing?', '[{"id":"a","label":"At 3-all"},{"id":"b","label":"Every game"},{"id":"c","label":"After the set ends"},{"id":"d","label":"At the agreed score, often 6-all"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'Many formats use a tiebreak at an agreed score such as 6-all.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-105', 'rookie', 'rules', 3, 'In junior drill scenario 95, what is the correct rule for standard tiebreak target?', '[{"id":"a","label":"At least seven points and a two-point lead"},{"id":"b","label":"Exactly seven points"},{"id":"c","label":"First to five"},{"id":"d","label":"First to ten only"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'A standard tiebreak is won at seven or more points with a two-point margin.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-106', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In junior drill scenario 96, what is the correct rule for doubles rally court?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Only singles sidelines count"},{"id":"b","label":"The doubles alleys count"},{"id":"c","label":"Only service boxes count"},{"id":"d","label":"Alleys count only on serves"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'In doubles rallies, the alleys are part of the court.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-107', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In junior drill scenario 97, what is the correct rule for doubles service game?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Partners switch every point"},{"id":"b","label":"Receiver picks the server"},{"id":"c","label":"One player serves the whole game"},{"id":"d","label":"Server changes after a fault"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'In doubles, one player serves for the whole game, then the team order continues in later service games.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-108', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In junior drill scenario 98, what is the correct rule for server steps on baseline early?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Let"},{"id":"b","label":"Legal serve"},{"id":"c","label":"Receiver hindrance"},{"id":"d","label":"Foot fault"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'A server may not touch the baseline or court before striking the serve.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-109', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In junior drill scenario 99, what is the correct rule for ball touches player?', '[{"id":"a","label":"That player loses the point"},{"id":"b","label":"Replay"},{"id":"c","label":"Opponent loses point"},{"id":"d","label":"Warning only"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'A player loses the point if the ball touches them or what they are wearing or carrying.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-11', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In club match scenario 1, what is the correct rule for zero points?', '[{"id":"a","label":"15"},{"id":"b","label":"30"},{"id":"c","label":"Love"},{"id":"d","label":"40"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'Zero points in tennis is called love.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-110', 'rookie', 'rules', 3, 'In junior drill scenario 100, what is the correct rule for deliberate distraction?', '[{"id":"a","label":"All distractions are ignored"},{"id":"b","label":"Deliberate hindrance can lose the point"},{"id":"c","label":"Always replay"},{"id":"d","label":"Only server can hinder"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'A deliberate hindrance can cause the player creating it to lose the point.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-111', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In doubles clinic scenario 101, what is the correct rule for zero points?', '[{"id":"a","label":"15"},{"id":"b","label":"30"},{"id":"c","label":"Love"},{"id":"d","label":"40"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'Zero points in tennis is called love.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-112', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In doubles clinic scenario 102, what is the correct rule for one point?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Love"},{"id":"b","label":"30"},{"id":"c","label":"40"},{"id":"d","label":"15"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'One point won in a standard game is called 15.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-113', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In doubles clinic scenario 103, what is the correct rule for two points?', '[{"id":"a","label":"30"},{"id":"b","label":"15"},{"id":"c","label":"40"},{"id":"d","label":"Advantage"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'Two points won in a standard game is called 30.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-114', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In doubles clinic scenario 104, what is the correct rule for three points?', '[{"id":"a","label":"30"},{"id":"b","label":"40"},{"id":"c","label":"45"},{"id":"d","label":"Game"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'Three points won in a standard game is called 40.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-115', 'rookie', 'rules', 3, 'In doubles clinic scenario 105, what is the correct rule for three points each?', '[{"id":"a","label":"30-all"},{"id":"b","label":"Advantage"},{"id":"c","label":"Deuce"},{"id":"d","label":"Game"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'When both players have three points, the score is deuce.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-116', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In doubles clinic scenario 106, what is the correct rule for one point after deuce?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Deuce"},{"id":"b","label":"Game"},{"id":"c","label":"Love"},{"id":"d","label":"Advantage"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'The point after deuce gives that player advantage.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-117', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In doubles clinic scenario 107, what is the correct rule for advantage is lost?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Back to deuce"},{"id":"b","label":"Game server"},{"id":"c","label":"Game receiver"},{"id":"d","label":"15-all"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'When the player with advantage loses the next point, the score returns to deuce.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-118', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In doubles clinic scenario 108, what is the correct rule for score-calling order?', '[{"id":"a","label":"The receiver’s score is called first"},{"id":"b","label":"The server’s score is called first"},{"id":"c","label":"The higher score is called first"},{"id":"d","label":"Either order is fine"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'The server’s score is always announced first in a game score.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-119', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In doubles clinic scenario 109, what is the correct rule for legal serve target?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Anywhere in singles court"},{"id":"b","label":"Straight ahead only"},{"id":"c","label":"In the diagonal service box"},{"id":"d","label":"Behind the baseline"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'A serve must land in the service box diagonally opposite the server.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-12', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In club match scenario 2, what is the correct rule for one point?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Love"},{"id":"b","label":"30"},{"id":"c","label":"40"},{"id":"d","label":"15"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'One point won in a standard game is called 15.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-120', 'rookie', 'rules', 3, 'In doubles clinic scenario 110, what is the correct rule for serve misses box?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Let"},{"id":"b","label":"Point server"},{"id":"c","label":"Point receiver"},{"id":"d","label":"Fault"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'A serve that misses the correct service box is a fault.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-121', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In doubles clinic scenario 111, what is the correct rule for two faults?', '[{"id":"a","label":"The server loses the point"},{"id":"b","label":"Third serve"},{"id":"c","label":"Replay"},{"id":"d","label":"Receiver chooses"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'Two faults on the same point make a double fault, so the server loses the point.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-122', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In doubles clinic scenario 112, what is the correct rule for serve clips net and lands in?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Server wins point"},{"id":"b","label":"Replay the serve"},{"id":"c","label":"Receiver wins point"},{"id":"d","label":"Replay game"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'A serve that touches the net and lands in the correct service box is a let and is replayed.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-123', 'rookie', 'rules', 1, 'In doubles clinic scenario 113, what is the correct rule for ball touches line?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Out"},{"id":"b","label":"Replay"},{"id":"c","label":"In"},{"id":"d","label":"Fault"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'A ball touching any part of the correct line is in.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-124', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In doubles clinic scenario 114, what is the correct rule for ball lands fully outside?', '[{"id":"a","label":"In"},{"id":"b","label":"Replay"},{"id":"c","label":"Let"},{"id":"d","label":"Out"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'A ball landing completely outside the relevant lines is out.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-125', 'rookie', 'rules', 3, 'In doubles clinic scenario 115, what is the correct rule for rally shot stays in net?', '[{"id":"a","label":"The hitter loses the point"},{"id":"b","label":"Replay"},{"id":"c","label":"Ball remains live"},{"id":"d","label":"Opponent loses point"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'A player loses the point when their shot does not cross the net into the opponent’s court.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
  ('rookie-126', 'rookie', 'rules', 2, 'In doubles clinic scenario 116, what is the correct rule for returning a serve?', '[{"id":"a","label":"Receiver may volley it"},{"id":"b","label":"The receiver must let the serve bounce"},{"id":"c","label":"Server may catch it"},{"id":"d","label":"It must bounce twice"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'The receiver must allow the serve to bounce before returning it.', null, 'ITF Rules of Tennis (2026)', 'https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/governance/rules-and-regulations/', true, false),
